codex
The current RGB GET arm reads only `buf[0..2]`, which reduces its affected-byte count. Also, zero-initialising the buffer would leave all four `random()` assignments intact; it would fix overlapping uninitialised bytes, not the random-colour behavior itself. I’m checking the memory-copy path and how callers propagate GET results.
